  "label": "The standalone word token \"info\" (abbreviation of information)",
  "positive_pole": "The token \"info\"/\"Info\" (with or without leading space, also \"-info\") used as a standalone word meaning information: \"more info\", \"any info\", \"Background info\", \"study.info\", \"Info Box\", \"Info Wars\". Weaker firing (~3) on the subword \"inf\" when it starts a longer word (inf-requent, inf-idel, Z-inf-andel, inf-raction, inf-estation, inf-using, inf-illing), and ~5 on \"Infos\" (Infosys). Faint (~1) on related abbreviation-like stems such as \"informative\", \"inform\", \"Prof\", \"intro\", \"summary\".",
  "negative_pole": "Negligible. Values bottom out at about -0.5 to -1 on scattered tokens such as \"JV\" and the suffix \"izers\". These can be treated as zero.",
