 {
  "k": 23,
  "layer": 0,
  "neuron": 8146,
  "label": "Uppercase acronym tokens starting with C/P/D-like letters (PCR, PCB, PC, CPR, DNA)",
  "positive_pole": "Single-token all-caps initialisms/acronyms, especially those beginning with P or C (PCR, PCB, PCA, PC/PCs, PVC, CPR, CDC, CQC, QC, GC, CD) plus DNA/mRNA. Activation sits on the acronym token itself, mostly when it is used as a noun or modifier in running text. PCR in a scientific methods context is strongest. A trailing piece such as 's' or 'R' after the main token gets a small spillover.",
  "negative_pole": "Negligible. There are faint values near -1 on 'that' in constructions like 'Not that\u2026', 'recognize that', 'see that', and on stray tokens like 'wan', 'RUN', 'Longer'. Treat these as at most -1.",
  "mono": 4,
  "windows": [
   {
    "kind": "held-out active",
    "tokens": [
     " specificity",
     " of",
     " PCR",
     ",\n",
     "but",
     " I",
