  "label": "Connectors inside category/eligibility qualifiers (+); health-insurance program names (\u2212)",
  "positive_pole": "Function-word and punctuation tokens (and, of, in, for, comma, slash, hyphen, 's, out, a/an) that sit inside a phrase specifying which category, group, level or place something belongs to. The neuron fires where a category label is expected next. Common settings are athletics and fitness, demographics, eligibility, places and insurance tiers. Examples: 'strength \u00aband\u00bb conditioning', '20 minutes \u00abof\u00bb strength training', 'women \u00abof\u00bb child-bearing age', 'NCAA Division \u00abI\u00bb \u00ab-\u00bb FBS', 'high school\u00ab/\u00bbcollege', 'student\u00ab-\u00bbathletes \u2026 intercollegiate \u00abor\u00bb professional', 'program \u00abfor\u00bb former football players', 'Boise \u00aband\u00bb Nampa', 'Salt Lake\u00ab,\u00bb Summit\u00ab,\u00bb Weber', 'LEESBURG\u00ab,\u00bb FLORIDA', 'in Portland\u00ab's\u00bb Southeast', 'transported \u00abto\u00bb Mercy Hospital', 'out \u00abof\u00bb college', 'paid \u00about\u00bb-of-pocket', '\u00about\u00bb of network', 'with \u00aban\u00bb HSA', 'General Women\u00ab's\u00bb Session', 'outstanding amateur athlete', 'three teams'. The token just before the qualifier carries the peak. Adjacent qualifier words get weaker activation (+1\u20133).",
